{"author":{"id":"3f8bad4585cb0f07c6570d9e31f06264af3b0abf48efbc5a44f56df5e7a9cd45"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789497526,"nonce":"Ls2lsCjvt2GPb/QgLhy3xJfOOUg=","message":"First increment landed in 26d2103 (with ash b42516a,\nBytecodeDecoder::decode_bytes):\n\n- caribou::bundle: the format (magic CARIBOU\\0, version, flags, a\n  manifest of name / entry / namespaces, then sections of kind, language,\n  format, name, bytes; all length-prefixed, no dependencies), emit and\n  load with unit tests; a set flag or an unknown version is refused.\n  Modelled on hatch's framing; the manifest is binary rather than TOML\n  since caribou build generates it from the project's layout and nobody\n  edits it.\n- caribou build \u003cprogram.hl\u003e [-o out]: the .hl as haxe/hl, every .wren\n  under the roots as wren/source named by its path under the root, the\n  namespaces from project::namespaces with the imports read off the\n  bytecode without loading (caribou_ash::imports_in). Written beside the\n  program as \u003cname\u003e.caribou.\n- Session::open reads the first bytes and opens a bundle as one: the\n  program from memory (caribou_ash::load_bytes, the bundle's path\n  standing in for the libraries beside it, argv[0] and the tier cache),\n  the world from the manifest's namespaces with no roots, World::install\n  handing each other module section to Adapter::install; the Wren\n  adapter stages sources (project::stage), consulted before the roots by\n  the loader and by plain imports. No watch for a bundle session.\n- Test: crates/caribou-interop/tests/bundle.rs (the hud project built\n  in-process, written to a temp dir, opened, same output as from the\n  directory); and `caribou run` of a bundle from an empty directory by\n  hand.\n\nNot in this increment: wlbc / .hatch module sections, resources reachable\nfrom a program, the Api sections (the two-layer schema of the original\ntext is largely covered by the registry, #export lines, `caribou\ndescribe` and the build macro; what a bundle would add is the\ninterfaces beside the modules for a reader that does not load them),\nNativeLib per target, Docs, compression, World::install of an entry that\nis not a Haxe hl program.","files":null}]}